  "claim_short": "In B(ell^2), let D e_n=e_(2n) and let the diagonal operator C have weight one on even coordinates and weight 1/n on coordinate 2n-1. Then CD=D is left invertible, while DC is not even left generalized Drazin invertible. Taking adjoints gives the right-sided failure. Thus Cline closure fails for left and right Drazin invertibility and for left and right generalized Drazin invertibility.",
